    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (76.67) and **Bryson Stott** (72.46) anchor the lineup as our most viable assets. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** is an elite start despite facing a lefty in Rod\u00f3n, as his dynamic platoon splits remain neutralized by his high base projection and favorable spot in the order. Similarly, **Bryson Stott** draws a premium matchup against a vulnerable Scherzer; his score is significantly elevated by an impressive +13% platoon edge, making him a high-floor play for runs and RBI. **Lawrence Butler** (66.94) also stands out as a strong start against Sproat, benefiting from the positive shift in his platoon profile to round out the top tier of our daily efficiency rankings.\n\nThe most challenging decision today involved the marginal starters in the 40\u201350 range. **Geraldo Perdomo** (44.86) and **Masyn Winn** (44.02) were the closest to cracking the starting nine, but both ultimately fell short due to their unfavorable matchups against pitchers with xERAs below 3.80. While speed is a priority for our strategy, the opportunity cost of starting them over **Gavin Sheets** (57.33) or **Taylor Ward** (55.54) was too high. **Taylor Ward** earns the nod despite the tough matchup against Kirby because the park factors provide a massive +16% boost to his output, keeping him well ahead of the bench candidates.\n\nWe are navigating a day with significant caution regarding lefty-on-lefty matchups. **Jonathan Aranda**, **Luis Arraez**, **Matt Chapman**, and **Jung Hoo Lee** are all staring down Griffin, which drags their scores toward the lower end of our efficiency spectrum. **Matt Chapman** (46.58) and **Luis Arraez** (45.30) remain in the lineup only due to their projected batting order significance, but these spots are high-risk. We will be monitoring the status of **Cal Raleigh** and **Will Smith** closely, as their absence due to injury and rest, respectively, limits our flexibility should any of these marginal starters underperform in their difficult matchups.",
